  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is Poparide available in the United States?</h3><p>No. Poparide operates across Canada but has never launched in the US. For city-to-city carpooling in the United States, regional cost-sharing marketplaces fill the same role — Seat Sherpa covers California and Nevada.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>What is the US version of Poparide?</h3><p>The closest US equivalent is a cost-sharing carpool marketplace like Seat Sherpa: drivers already making an intercity trip post their empty seats, prices are capped at the real cost of the drive, and payment is held in-app until pickup is confirmed.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Can I use Poparide in California?</h3><p>No — Poparide has no California network. Seat Sherpa covers California's main routes (SF–LA, LA–San Diego, LA–Las Vegas and more) on the same cost-sharing model.</p></div>

